    {
      "id": 160885,
      "name": "Foote",
      "username": "Foote",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-09T20:15:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Flib\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/a8b319/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Flib:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Thanks. I picked up some mini expansions today at the local boardgame store, and didn't notice that they were for Villains. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>There are no mini-expansions that are for \"Villains of the Multiverse\" or the Vengance format. This might&nbsp;cause confusion by putting it that way.&nbsp;Any mini-expansions are just that and are playable just like any normal game of SotM would be. Wager Master wasn't even released during th VotM cycle = D</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:41:24.002Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
