      "id": 160888,
      "name": "Craig",
      "username": "Craig",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/craig/{size}/2150_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-09T20:52:07.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><strong>Flib wrote:</strong><br><blockquote>Foote wrote:<br><blockquote>&nbsp;Flib wrote:<br><blockquote>Thanks. I picked up some mini expansions today at the local boardgame store, and didn't notice that they were for Villains. :)&nbsp;&nbsp;</blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></div>\nThere are no mini-expansions that are for \"Villains of the Multiverse\" or the Vengance format. This might&nbsp;cause confusion by putting it that way.&nbsp;Any mini-expansions are just that and are playable just like any normal game of SotM would be. Wager Master wasn't even released during th VotM cycle = D\n<p>&nbsp;Yes, that is confusing. After all, it's a mini expansion that has \"villains of the multiverse\" written on it.</p>\n<p>What? It says that?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I can confirm that no mini expansion says \"Villains of the Multiverse\" on it. The say \"Sentinels of the Multiverse\" at the top, and say whether they are a Hero, Villain, or Environment.</p>",
